; .c already lies on --ac, so the identity landing is dropped and the mirror
; landing (-1, -1) leaves one crease: the anti-diagonal direction through .a.
; It touches the sheet at the corner .a alone and creases nothing, so the
; paper-incidence filter leaves no survivor and there is no fold to make.

paper square
--ac = through .a .c
--x = map .c onto --ac through .a

; expect error "map .c onto --ac through .a: no crease lands on the paper — no fold to make"
